--- Diagnosis ---
error_code: REDMINE_WRITE_FORBIDDEN (authorization class, HTTP 401/403 equivalent)
Evidence:
  * All POST /issues attempts rejected with the same permission error (5 distinct payloads + 1 retry) -> not payload-dependent.
  * GET /users/current.json (kind=me) also rejected -> token-level scope limitation, not tracker/priority misconfiguration.
  * Read endpoints (projects, trackers, priorities, issues) work -> API key is valid but lacks write/troubleshoot scope.
  * Trackers verified as enabled in project "login": #1 TestCase, #2 Task. Priorities verified: #1 Minor, #2 Major, #3 Critical.
Conclusion: publication of test cases is impossible with the currently configured credentials. Cause is environmental (permissions), not a defect of the test model.

